He did not say how big he wanted it to scale.  For the values he gave
(vector of 1000) this is only using 8MB of memory and it is fast.  I agree
that if he has vector longer than about 4000 (using 128MB at that point),
you might want to look at some other approach.  Even then, if you can scale
them to integers, you use only 1/2 the memory.  It all depends on what
problem he is trying to solve.

