From ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk  Tue Apr  8 14:34:15 2003
From: ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk (Prof Brian Ripley)
Date: Tue, 08 Apr 2003 15:34:15 +0100
Subject: Re: summing absolute differences (was For posting to S-News)
In-Reply-To: <C9E4E43770853445A93F5DFA2742532F318CCA@MAIL2.joslin.harvard.edu>
References: <C9E4E43770853445A93F5DFA2742532F318CCA@MAIL2.joslin.harvard.edu>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.44.0304081526000.6665-100000@gannet.stats>

How long is the vector?

sum(abs(outer(V, V, "-"))) is the most obvious way, and will be fast 
provided here is enough memory to store all pairs.  (You may perhaps have 
meant only half the pairs and hence half the sum).

Another idea is sum(dist(as.matrix(V)) since you are considering Euclidean 
distances.

For a vector of length 1000 I got 0.46 and 0.15secs respectively.  If that 
