Dear Ken:

	  Have you considered using "synchronize()" to store progress up to the 
point of failure?

	  Do you think it might be a "garbage collection" problem?  I don't 
know about S-Plus 6.1, but I know that previous releases had memory 
leaks.  If you store progress as you go, you can then just restart from 
the point of failure.  I had multiple computers running for months with 
an extensive set of computer simulations, reporting regularly the time 
taken in the last iteration.  I had to kill it and restart every day or 
two, because otherwise, the time per iteration would go to Inf.

	  Also, have you tried the same thing in R?  There are a few things 
that don't work in one of R and S-Plus but do work in the other.

hope this helps.  spencer graves

